[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337525444,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337575754,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337579424,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337581724,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337583644,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337585744,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337587584,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337589374,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337591184,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337592994,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337595224,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337597414,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below 12 qubits (8 with mid-circuit measurement), and the CI gate shards (`kaggle_run.py shards`) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337600524,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches 12 qubits, or 8 with mid-circuit measurement (docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md, \"CPU against T4\") | IBM jobs; narrow replays, which the T4 speeds up by at most 3 times |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337602914,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337604924,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. An account without Persona identity verification gets a 4-core CPU machine for every TPU request; a verified account's request queues for a TPU, one batch session at a time (docs/notes/kaggle/tpu-research.md) | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337607254,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337609294,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337611334,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337613304,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337615434,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337617214,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337619024,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337622334,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337624314,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337626144,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337627954,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337629874,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337638974,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337641054,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack, built and proved by\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337643024,"data":"   `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`. `--fetch` downloads the seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337644934,"data":"   archives `RELEASES` pins and keeps each only if its sha256 matches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337646814,"data":"   `--install` installs sixteen of them with `pip install --no-deps`,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337648764,"data":"   applying `BUILD_RECIPES` (the cayley-dickson, SplitOct and pyquaternion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337650644,"data":"   PKGBUILD `prepare()` steps) and taking the Octonion-Sedenion wheel as\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337652524,"data":"   published, then installs `RUNTIME_PINS`: numpy-quaternion, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337654414,"data":"   seventeenth, as its pinned compiled wheel, and numba, sparse and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337656304,"data":"   anywidget. `--extract` binds all seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337658254,"data":"   installed distributions to their archives and regenerates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337660134,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json`; the kernel stops with exit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337662024,"data":"   code 3 unless those bytes equal the retained ones. The build host passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337663904,"data":"   the same test against its Arch packages, so a run that reaches its entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337665784,"data":"   used the same algebra code as the host. The file's `packages` field\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337667664,"data":"   records the versions `kernel_main.REPORTED_PACKAGES` names, nine of the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337669544,"data":"   seventeen algebra distributions; the byte comparison binds the rest.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337671414,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337673314,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337675114,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337676984,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337678754,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337680564,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337682324,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337684174,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337685964,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337687804,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337689874,"data":"| cuquantum-cu11 | 24.8.0 (brings custatevec-cu11 1.6.0.post1 and cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0; the libraries the cu11 Aer wheel links) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337691934,"data":"| cutensor-cu11 | 2.2.0 (the newest release inside cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0's `\u003e=2.0.1,\u003c3`) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337694614,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337696614,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337701324,"data":"| quaternionic, clifford, kingdon, galgebra, pyoctonion | 1.0.18, 1.5.1, 3.0.0, 0.6.0, 3.12 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337703394,"data":"| pyquaternion | 0.9.9 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe (writes the VERSION.txt the sdist omits) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337705364,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337707304,"data":"| hyprat | 0.2.0 | GitHub tag archive, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337709184,"data":"| Octonion-Sedenion | 1.0.0 | PyPI wheel (its only release form), sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337711224,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI compiled wheel at the pin; `--extract` binds its Python files to the sha256-pinned sdist (Octonion-Sedenion builds on it) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337713744,"data":"| numba, sparse, anywidget | 0.68.0, 0.17.0, 0.11.0 | PyPI (`RUNTIME_PINS`; runtime dependencies of quaternionic, clifford and kingdon) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337716434,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337719674,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337722704,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337724754,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337726704,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337728524,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337730434,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337732324,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337734184,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337736094,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337737904,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337739764,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337741664,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337743464,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337745354,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337747174,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337749054,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337750924,"data":"- An entry whose output a CI gate recompiles runs with `push --ci-env` on a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337752844,"data":"  CPU or GPU machine, using CPU Aer either way. The kernel then builds CI's Python 3.14.7 with CI's pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337755484,"data":"  through `ci/install_pins.sh` and runs the entry under it, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337757434,"data":"  image's Python 3.13 and numpy 2.1.3 change compiled depths and durations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337761794,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337763664,"data":"## Aer on the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337765504,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337767274,"data":"- **Requesting a GPU.** Push with `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4` and a `--timeout`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337769164,"data":"  sized to the work; kaggle_run.py refuses an accelerator push without one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337771044,"data":"  The kernel installs qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 0.17.2, cuquantum-cu11 24.8.0 and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337772954,"data":"  cutensor-cu11 2.2.0 and sets `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE=GPU`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337774904,"data":"- **cuStateVec.** `noise_simulator(..., custatevec=True)` sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337776774,"data":"  `cuStateVec_enable` on a GPU statevector run; `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337778664,"data":"  --only cpu_statevector gpu_statevector gpu_statevector_custatevec` records\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337780694,"data":"  the three paths with Aer's reported `cuStateVec_enable`. The option excludes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337782594,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`. `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` holds the library\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337784504,"data":"  chain, the T4 push command and how to read its result.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337786384,"data":"- **Using it in an entry.** The entry passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337788214,"data":"  `calibration_snapshot.aer_device()` to `noise_simulator(snapshot, device,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337790134,"data":"  method=...)`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337791974,"data":"- **Noise model width.** Restricting the snapshot and the circuit to the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337793863999998,"data":"  active qubits (`snapshot_laws.restrict` and `restrict_circuit`) keeps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337795754,"data":"  Aer's noise model at the circuit's width on either device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337797624,"data":"- **What the GPU is for.** It pays for density matrices at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337799494,"data":"  `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` (11) qubits or more and for wide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337801364,"data":"  statevectors. Small dynamic circuits sample faster on the host CPUs. On\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337803224,"data":"  the 7-qubit N=21 order-finding circuits, statevector trajectories took 2.8\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337805104,"data":"  and 36 ms per shot on the CPU, against 21.7 and 54.6 ms on one T4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337806974,"data":"- **Batched shots.** `noise_simulator(..., batched_shots=True)` enables Aer's\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337808854,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`, which aborts on any circuit with control flow\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337811264,"data":"  (`if_else` lowers to `jump`), so only static circuits may batch. Batched\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337813154,"data":"  static runs are unmeasured here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337814984,"data":"- **Replay.** A GPU's seeded counts differ from the CPU's. Its records are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337816844,"data":"  replayed from their retained counts, never by resampling on CI.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337818714,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337820474,"data":"The measurements are in `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`, from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337824804,"data":"`results/kaggle/2026-10-16T204620Z-gororoba-aer-gpu-probe`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18.337826814,"data":"\n"}
